IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spc-nouns`
IMPORT `spc-dates`
IMPORT `spc-part-interpretation`
IMPORT `spc-part-misc`
IMPORT `spc-part-final`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, "State pension credit: entitlement and
-- amount" (sections 1 to 5, with section 3ZA) and the definition of "entitled" in
-- section 17(1), which calls them.
--
-- WHAT THE RULES TAKE. Each rule takes the `Case` (one claimant on one day) and,
-- where an amount is read, the `Prescribed` record holding the figures the Act
-- leaves to regulations. Every figure is an input; the tests use invented ones.
--
-- RULE ORDER AND NAMES. Rules follow the Act's own order. Each name starts with
-- the section it encodes, so no name is defined twice across the modules.
--
-- ARM ORDER AND PRIORITY. The Act says in section 1(4) that subsections (2) and
-- (3) are "subject to the following provisions of this Act". Those provisions are
-- section 3ZA (a savings credit is refused in a prescribed mixed-age couple case)
-- and section 4(1), (1A) and (2) (three exclusions from state pension credit
-- altogether). Section 4(3) does not remove entitlement; it stops payment of an
-- amount below a prescribed figure. The exclusions are therefore applied to
-- entitlement, and section 4(3) to what is payable.
--
-- NOT COVERED. Sections 12 and 18A let regulations (and pilot schemes) displace or
-- modify provisions of this Act. If either reaches the case, the Act's own rules
-- cannot be said to decide it, and the rules that answer a question return
-- `Not covered by this encoding` (an Answer) or NOTHING (a MAYBE NUMBER).

§ `State pension credit: entitlement and amount`

§§ `1 Entitlement`

-- Section 1(5)(a), (b): regulations may say when a person is treated as being, or
-- not being, in Great Britain, and may continue entitlement during temporary
-- absence. The first is already counted in the input `in Great Britain`. The
-- second is a separate way of satisfying section 1(2)(a): a claimant who is not in
-- Great Britain at the time but whose entitlement the regulations continue.
-- src:9 | (a) he is in Great Britain;
-- src:19 | (5) Regulations may make provision for the purposes of this Act—
-- src:20 | (a) as to circumstances in which a person is to be treated as being or not being in Great Britain; or
-- src:21 | (b) continuing a person’s entitlement to state pension credit during periods of temporary absence from Great Britain.
@ref s 1(2)(a); s 1(5)(a), (b) (src:9; src:19-21)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(2)(a) -- he is in Great Britain` case MEANS
        case's `in Great Britain`
    OR  case's `temporarily absent from Great Britain and entitlement continued by regulations`

-- Section 1(2)(b): "has attained the qualifying age", worked out by section 1(6).
-- src:10 | (b) he has attained the qualifying age; and
@ref s 1(2)(b) (src:10)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(2)(b) -- he has attained the qualifying age` case MEANS
    `s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (case's `day tested`) (case's claimant)

-- Section 1(2)(c): he satisfies the guarantee credit condition (section 2(1)) or
-- the savings credit conditions (section 3(1) and (2)). Section 3ZA is applied to
-- the second route, because subsection (4) makes section 1(2) subject to it: a
-- person who section 3ZA says is not entitled to a savings credit has no
-- savings-credit route to state pension credit (fork F-03, NOTES.md).
-- src:11 | (c) he satisfies—
-- src:12 | (i) the condition in section 2(1) (guarantee credit); or
-- src:13 | (ii) the conditions in section 3(1) and (2) (savings credit).
@ref s 1(2)(c) (src:11-13)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(2)(c) -- he satisfies the guarantee credit condition or the savings credit conditions` case prescribed MEANS
        "(i) the condition in section 2(1) (guarantee credit);" ... `s 2(1) -- the guarantee credit condition` case prescribed
    OR  "(ii) the conditions in section 3(1) and (2) (savings credit)." ...
            (       `s 3(1) -- the first savings credit condition` case
                AND `s 3(2) -- the second savings credit condition` case prescribed
                AND NOT (`s 3ZA(1) -- not entitled to a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple` case) )

-- Section 1(2) as a whole: all three of (a), (b) and (c).
-- src:8 | (2) A claimant is entitled to state pension credit if—
@ref s 1(2) (src:8)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(2) -- the conditions of section 1(2) are met` case prescribed MEANS
        "(a) he is in Great Britain;" ... `s 1(2)(a) -- he is in Great Britain` case
    ... "(b) he has attained the qualifying age; and" ... `s 1(2)(b) -- he has attained the qualifying age` case
    AND "(c) he satisfies (i) or (ii)" ... `s 1(2)(c) -- he satisfies the guarantee credit condition or the savings credit conditions` case prescribed

-- Section 1(4): subsections (2) and (3) are subject to the following provisions of
-- the Act. The exclusions that remove entitlement to state pension credit
-- altogether are section 4(1), 4(1A) and 4(2); they are applied here, to the
-- Act's own test of entitlement. (Section 3ZA is applied inside section 1(2)(c).)
-- src:18 | (4) Subsections (2) and (3) are subject to the following provisions of this Act.
@ref s 1(4) (src:18)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed MEANS
        `s 1(2) -- the conditions of section 1(2) are met` case prescribed
    AND NOT (`s 4(1) -- excluded because the other member of the couple is entitled` case)
    AND NOT (`s 4(1A) -- excluded because the other member of the couple has not attained the qualifying age` case)
    AND NOT (`s 4(2) -- excluded under section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` case)

-- Sections 12 and 18A: regulations (and pilot schemes) may displace or modify the
-- provisions of this Act. Where either reaches the case, nothing in the Act, as
-- encoded, decides it.
@ref s 1(4); s 12(1); s 18A(5) (src:18)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` case MEANS
        `s 12(1) -- section 12 applies to the case` case
    OR  `s 18A(5) -- a pilot scheme may displace provisions of the Act for the case` case

-- Section 1(3)(a): entitled to a guarantee credit if entitled to state pension
-- credit and he satisfies the condition in section 2(1).
-- src:14 | (3) A claimant who is entitled to state pension credit is entitled—
-- src:15 | (a) to a guarantee credit, calculated in accordance with section 2, if he satisfies the condition in subsection (1) of that section, or
@ref s 1(3)(a) (src:14-15)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(3)(a) -- entitled to a guarantee credit` case prescribed MEANS
        `s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed
    AND `s 2(1) -- the guarantee credit condition` case prescribed

-- Section 1(3)(b): entitled to a savings credit if entitled to state pension
-- credit and he satisfies the conditions in section 3(1) and (2), unless section 3ZA
-- refuses it.
-- src:16 | (b) to a savings credit, calculated in accordance with section 3, if he satisfies the conditions in subsections (1) and (2) of that section,
-- src:17 | (or to both, if he satisfies both the condition mentioned in paragraph (a) and the conditions mentioned in paragraph (b)).
@ref s 1(3)(b) (src:16-17)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(3)(b) -- entitled to a savings credit` case prescribed MEANS
        `s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed
    AND `s 3(1) -- the first savings credit condition` case
    AND `s 3(2) -- the second savings credit condition` case prescribed
    AND NOT (`s 3ZA(1) -- not entitled to a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple` case)

-- Section 1(6): "the qualifying age" is pensionable age for a woman, and for a man
-- the age which is pensionable age for a woman born on the same day as the man.
-- Pensionable age is not defined by this Act (section 17(1) hands it to paragraph 1
-- of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995, not among the inputs), so the day each
-- age is attained is a fact in the `Person` record. For a woman the two facts are
-- the same day by definition.
-- src:22 | (6) In this Act “the qualifying age” means—
-- src:23 | (a) in the case of a woman, pensionable age; or
-- src:24 | (b) in the case of a man, the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day as the man.
@ref s 1(6) (src:22-24)
GIVEN person IS A Person
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1(6) -- the day the person attains the qualifying age` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person's sex
        WHEN Woman THEN person's `day pensionable age is attained`
        WHEN Man THEN person's `day a woman born on the same day attains pensionable age`

@ref s 1(6) (src:22-24)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      person IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` day person MEANS
    day AT LEAST `s 1(6) -- the day the person attains the qualifying age` person

-- Section 1(1) says a benefit known as state pension credit is payable in
-- accordance with the provisions that follow. It states no condition.
-- src:7 | (1) A social security benefit to be known as state pension credit shall be payable in accordance with the following provisions of this Act.
-- (not encoded: section 1(1) introduces the benefit; the conditions are in section 1(2) onwards)

§§ `2 Guarantee credit`

-- Section 2(5): the standard minimum guarantee is a uniform single amount for every
-- claimant who is a member of a couple, and a lower uniform single amount for every
-- claimant who is not. Section 2(4): both are prescribed amounts (inputs).
-- src:35 | (4) The standard minimum guarantee shall be a prescribed amount.
-- src:36 | (5) The standard minimum guarantee shall be—
-- src:37 | (a) a uniform single amount in the case of every claimant who is a member of a couple ; and
-- src:38 | (b) a lower uniform single amount in the case of every claimant who is not a member of a couple .
@ref s 2(4), (5) (src:35-38)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(5) -- the standard minimum guarantee` case prescribed MEANS
    IF `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
    THEN prescribed's `standard minimum guarantee for a member of a couple`
    ELSE prescribed's `standard minimum guarantee for a claimant who is not a member of a couple`

-- Section 2(6): regulations may provide that, in prescribed cases, the reference
-- in subsection (3)(a) to the standard minimum guarantee is replaced by a
-- prescribed amount. JUST the amount in a prescribed case, NOTHING otherwise.
-- The substitution is made in section 2(3)(a) only; section 3(7)(a) reads the
-- standard minimum guarantee itself (fork F-05, NOTES.md).
-- src:39 | (6) Regulations may provide that, in prescribed cases, subsection (3) shall have effect with the substitution for the reference in paragraph (a) to the standard minimum guarantee of a reference to a prescribed amount.
@ref s 2(6) (src:39)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(3)(a) -- the amount that stands for the standard minimum guarantee in the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed MEANS
    CONSIDER prescribed's `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee`
        WHEN JUST substitute THEN substitute
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 2(5) -- the standard minimum guarantee` case prescribed

-- Section 2(8): an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits
-- Act (or carer support payment) to the claimant, or, if the claimant is a member
-- of a couple, to the other member, adds ONE amount "in respect of that
-- circumstance", however many of them have it (fork F-06, NOTES.md).
-- src:41 | (8) Where—
-- src:42 | (a) the claimant is entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or carer support payment , or
-- src:43 | (b) if the claimant is a member of a couple , the other member of the couple is entitled to such an allowance or payment ,
-- src:44 | there shall be included among the additional amounts prescribed under subsection (3)(b) an amount in respect of that circumstance.
@ref s 2(8) (src:41-44)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` case MEANS
        "(a) the claimant is entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or carer support payment, or" ... case's `claimant entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment`
    OR  "(b) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple is entitled to such an allowance or payment," ...
            (       `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
                AND case's `other member entitled to an allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act or to carer support payment` )

-- Section 2(3)(b), (7), (8): the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable.
-- Severe disability adds the amount in subsection (7); the allowance in subsection
-- (8) adds its amount; the rest are the other additional amounts regulations
-- prescribe (an input, which is nil where none applies: subsection (9)).
-- src:34 | (b) such prescribed additional amounts as may be applicable.
-- src:40 | (7) Where the claimant is severely disabled, there shall be included among the additional amounts prescribed under subsection (3)(b) an amount in respect of that circumstance.
@ref s 2(3)(b), (7) (src:34; src:40)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` case prescribed MEANS
        IF case's `severely disabled`
        THEN prescribed's `additional amount for a claimant who is severely disabled`
        ELSE 0
    PLUS IF `s 2(8) -- an amount is included for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment` case
         THEN prescribed's `additional amount for an allowance under section 70 or carer support payment`
         ELSE 0
    PLUS prescribed's `other prescribed additional amounts that are applicable`

-- Section 2(3): the appropriate minimum guarantee is the total of the standard
-- minimum guarantee (or the amount substituted for it) and the applicable
-- prescribed additional amounts.
-- src:32 | (3) The appropriate minimum guarantee shall be the total of—
-- src:33 | (a) the standard minimum guarantee; and
-- src:34 | (b) such prescribed additional amounts as may be applicable.
@ref s 2(3) (src:32-34)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed MEANS
        `s 2(3)(a) -- the amount that stands for the standard minimum guarantee in the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed
    PLUS `s 2(3)(b) -- the prescribed additional amounts that are applicable` case prescribed

-- Section 2(1): the condition is that the claimant has no income, or has income
-- which does not exceed the appropriate minimum guarantee. The income is the
-- claimant's own plus, in a couple, the other member's (section 5).
-- src:26 | (1) The condition mentioned in section 1(2)(c)(i) is that the claimant—
-- src:27 | (a) has no income; or
-- src:28 | (b) has income which does not exceed the appropriate minimum guarantee.
@ref s 2(1) (src:26-28)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) -- the guarantee credit condition` case prescribed MEANS
        "(a) has no income; or" ... `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case EQUALS 0
    OR  "(b) has income which does not exceed the appropriate minimum guarantee." ... `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case AT MOST `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed

-- Section 2(2): where the claimant is entitled to a guarantee credit, it is the
-- appropriate minimum guarantee if there is no income, and otherwise the
-- difference between the appropriate minimum guarantee and the income.
-- src:29 | (2) Where the claimant is entitled to a guarantee credit, then—
-- src:30 | (a) if he has no income, the guarantee credit shall be the appropriate minimum guarantee; and
-- src:31 | (b) if he has income, the guarantee credit shall be the difference between the appropriate minimum guarantee and his income.
@ref s 2(2) (src:29-31)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(2) -- the guarantee credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed MEANS
    IF `s 1(3)(a) -- entitled to a guarantee credit` case prescribed
    THEN BRANCH
            IF `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case EQUALS 0
            THEN `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed
            OTHERWISE `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed MINUS `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case
    ELSE 0

-- Section 2(9): the powers to prescribe amounts include power to prescribe nil,
-- except for the standard minimum guarantee. Nothing to encode: every prescribed
-- amount in `Prescribed` is a plain number that may be 0, and the standard minimum
-- guarantee is the one the tests never set to 0.
-- src:45 | (9) Except for the amount of the standard minimum guarantee, the powers conferred by this section to prescribe amounts include power to prescribe nil as an amount.
-- (not encoded as a rule: section 2(9) permits nil amounts; any input may be 0)

§§ `3 Savings credit`

-- Section 3(1)(a): "has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has
-- attained the age of 65 (before, on or after that date)". Two different dates:
-- the day pensionable age was attained must be BEFORE 6 April 2016 (so the day
-- itself is out); the age of 65 is tested on the day tested. Pensionable age here
-- is the person's own, not the qualifying age of section 1(6) (they differ for a man).
-- src:47 | (1) The first of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(c)(ii) is that the claimant—
-- src:48 | (a) has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65 (before, on or after that date), or
@ref s 3(1)(a) (src:47-48)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      person IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` day person MEANS
        person's `day pensionable age is attained` LESS THAN `6 April 2016`
    AND `the age has been attained on` day `by a person born on` (person's `date of birth`) `at the age of` `the age of 65`

-- Section 3(1): the first condition is (a) the claimant satisfies paragraph (a), or
-- (b) the claimant is a member of a couple and the other member satisfies it.
-- src:47 | (1) The first of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(c)(ii) is that the claimant—
-- src:48 | (a) has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65 (before, on or after that date), or
-- src:49 | (b) is a member of a couple, the other member of which falls within paragraph (a).
@ref s 3(1) (src:47-49)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) -- the first savings credit condition` case MEANS
        "(a) has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65 (before, on or after that date), or" ... `s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` (case's `day tested`) (case's claimant)
    OR  "(b) is a member of a couple, the other member of which falls within paragraph (a)." ...
            (       `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
                AND `s 3(1)(a) -- has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65` (case's `day tested`) (case's `other member of the couple`) )

-- Section 3(7): the maximum savings credit is a prescribed percentage of the
-- difference between the standard minimum guarantee and the savings credit
-- threshold. Section 3(8): regulations may prescribe descriptions of persons for
-- whom it is taken to be nil. The standard minimum guarantee here is the one of
-- section 2(5), not the amount substituted under section 2(6) (fork F-05).
-- src:63 | (7) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:64 | “the savings credit threshold” is such amount as may be prescribed;
-- src:65 | “the maximum savings credit” is a prescribed percentage of the difference between—
-- src:66 | (a) the standard minimum guarantee; and
-- src:67 | (b) the savings credit threshold.
-- src:68 | (8) Regulations may prescribe descriptions of persons in whose case the maximum savings credit shall be taken to be nil.
@ref s 3(7), (8) (src:63-68)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(7) -- the maximum savings credit` case prescribed MEANS
    IF case's `regulations under section 3(8) take the maximum savings credit to be nil`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (prescribed's `prescribed percentage for the maximum savings credit`
          TIMES (`s 2(5) -- the standard minimum guarantee` case prescribed MINUS prescribed's `savings credit threshold`))
         DIVIDED BY 100

-- Section 3(4), amount A: the smaller of the maximum savings credit and a
-- prescribed percentage of the amount by which the claimant's qualifying income
-- exceeds the savings credit threshold. Where the qualifying income does not exceed
-- the threshold there is no such excess and the second limb is taken as nil
-- (section 3(2)(a) will already have refused the savings credit).
-- src:54 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3)—
-- src:55 | “amount A” is the smaller of—
-- src:56 | (a) the maximum savings credit; and
-- src:57 | (b) a prescribed percentage of the amount by which the claimant’s qualifying income exceeds the savings credit threshold; and
@ref s 3(4) (src:54-57)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(4) -- amount A` case prescribed MEANS
    min (`s 3(7) -- the maximum savings credit` case prescribed)
        ((prescribed's `prescribed percentage for amount A`
          TIMES max 0 (`s 5 -- the qualifying income treated as the claimant's` case MINUS prescribed's `savings credit threshold`))
         DIVIDED BY 100)

-- Section 3(5): where by regulations under section 2(6) the claimant's appropriate
-- minimum guarantee does not include the standard minimum guarantee, regulations
-- may provide that the reference in amount B to the appropriate minimum guarantee is
-- replaced by a prescribed higher amount. It applies only if BOTH the section 2(6)
-- substitution is in play AND the section 3(5) regulations give a higher amount.
-- src:61 | (5) Where, by virtue of regulations under section 2(6), the claimant’s appropriate minimum guarantee does not include the standard minimum guarantee, regulations may provide that the definition of “amount B” in subsection (4) shall have effect with the substitution for the reference in paragraph (a) to the appropriate minimum guarantee of a reference to a prescribed higher amount.
@ref s 3(5) (src:61)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` case prescribed MEANS
    CONSIDER prescribed's `prescribed amount substituted for the standard minimum guarantee`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed
        WHEN JUST substitute THEN
            CONSIDER prescribed's `prescribed higher amount substituted for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B`
                WHEN JUST higher THEN higher
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 2(3) -- the appropriate minimum guarantee` case prescribed

-- Section 3(4), amount B: a prescribed percentage of the amount (if any) by which
-- the claimant's income exceeds the appropriate minimum guarantee; if there is no
-- such excess, nil. Income here is the whole income of section 15(1), not the
-- qualifying income.
-- src:58 | “amount B” is—
-- src:59 | (a) a prescribed percentage of the amount (if any) by which the claimant’s income exceeds the appropriate minimum guarantee; or
-- src:60 | (b) if there is no such excess, nil.
@ref s 3(4) (src:58-60)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(4) -- amount B` case prescribed MEANS
    IF `s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case GREATER THAN `s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` case prescribed
    THEN (prescribed's `prescribed percentage for amount B`
          TIMES (`s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case MINUS `s 3(5) -- the figure that stands for the appropriate minimum guarantee in amount B` case prescribed))
         DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

-- Section 3(2): the second condition is (a) the claimant's qualifying income
-- exceeds the savings credit threshold, and (b) amount A exceeds amount B.
-- src:50 | (2) The second of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(c)(ii) is that—
-- src:51 | (a) the claimant’s qualifying income exceeds the savings credit threshold; and
-- src:52 | (b) the claimant’s income is such that, for the purposes of subsection (3), amount A exceeds amount B.
@ref s 3(2) (src:50-52)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) -- the second savings credit condition` case prescribed MEANS
        "(a) the claimant's qualifying income exceeds the savings credit threshold; and" ... `s 5 -- the qualifying income treated as the claimant's` case GREATER THAN prescribed's `savings credit threshold`
    AND "(b) the claimant's income is such that, for the purposes of subsection (3), amount A exceeds amount B." ... `s 3(4) -- amount A` case prescribed GREATER THAN `s 3(4) -- amount B` case prescribed

-- Section 3(3): where the claimant is entitled to a savings credit, it is the
-- amount by which amount A exceeds amount B.
-- src:53 | (3) Where the claimant is entitled to a savings credit, the amount of the savings credit shall be the amount by which amount A exceeds amount B.
@ref s 3(3) (src:53)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 3(3) -- the savings credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed MEANS
    IF `s 1(3)(b) -- entitled to a savings credit` case prescribed
    THEN `s 3(4) -- amount A` case prescribed MINUS `s 3(4) -- amount B` case prescribed
    ELSE 0

-- Section 3(6): regulations say what income counts as qualifying income. The
-- qualifying income of each member is an input (`Case`), stated as the regulations
-- work it out.
-- src:62 | (6) Regulations may make provision as to income which is, and income which is not, to be treated as qualifying income for the purposes of this section.
-- (not encoded: section 3(6) is a power to make regulations; qualifying income is an input)

§§ `3ZA Power to limit savings credit for certain mixed-age couples`

-- Section 3ZA(3): a mixed-age couple is a couple (whenever formed) one member of
-- which had attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and the other had not.
-- This looks at 6 April 2016 only, not at the day tested, and at pensionable age
-- (each person's own), not the qualifying age.
-- src:74 | (3) In this section “mixed-age couple” means a couple (whenever formed) one member of which had attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and the other had not.
@ref s 3ZA(3) (src:74)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3ZA(3) -- the claimant is a member of a mixed-age couple` case MEANS
        `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
    AND (   (    case's claimant's `day pensionable age is attained` LESS THAN `6 April 2016`
             AND NOT (case's `other member of the couple`'s `day pensionable age is attained` LESS THAN `6 April 2016`) )
         OR (    case's `other member of the couple`'s `day pensionable age is attained` LESS THAN `6 April 2016`
             AND NOT (case's claimant's `day pensionable age is attained` LESS THAN `6 April 2016`) ) )

-- Section 3ZA(1): regulations may provide that, in prescribed cases, a member of a
-- mixed-age couple is not entitled to a savings credit. Whether the regulations
-- reach the claimant's case is an input (the Act states no case).
-- src:70 | (1) Regulations may provide that, in prescribed cases, a person who is a member of a mixed-age couple is not entitled to a savings credit.
@ref s 3ZA(1) (src:70)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3ZA(1) -- not entitled to a savings credit as a member of a mixed-age couple` case MEANS
        `s 3ZA(3) -- the claimant is a member of a mixed-age couple` case
    AND case's `regulations under section 3ZA(1) prescribe the claimant's case`

-- Section 3ZA(2) is an example of what the regulations could provide ("For
-- example, the regulations could provide ..."), not a rule. It is not encoded.
-- src:71 | (2) For example, the regulations could provide that a member of a mixed-age couple is not entitled to a savings credit unless—
-- src:72 | (a) the person has been awarded a savings credit with effect from a day before 6 April 2016 and was entitled to a savings credit immediately before that date, and
-- src:73 | (b) the person remained entitled to state pension credit at all times since the beginning of 6 April 2016.
-- (not encoded: section 3ZA(2) gives an example of what regulations could say)

§§ `4 Exclusions`

-- Section 4(1): a claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if a member of
-- a couple the other member of which is entitled to state pension credit.
-- "Entitled" is the defined word (section 17(1)). Whether the other member IS
-- entitled is a fact the claimant states; the encoding never works it out from the
-- claimant's own entitlement, which would be circular (fork F-07).
-- src:76 | (1) A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which is entitled to state pension credit.
@ref s 4(1) (src:76)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) -- excluded because the other member of the couple is entitled` case MEANS
        `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
    AND case's `other member entitled to state pension credit`

-- Section 4(1A): a claimant is not entitled if a member of a couple the other
-- member of which has not attained the qualifying age.
-- src:77 | (1A) A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not attained the qualifying age.
@ref s 4(1A) (src:77)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1A) -- excluded because the other member of the couple has not attained the qualifying age` case MEANS
        `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
    AND NOT (`s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (case's `day tested`) (case's `other member of the couple`))

-- Section 4(2) amends section 115(1) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 so
-- that a person excluded by that section from the benefits it lists is also
-- excluded from state pension credit. The amendment's text is not a rule in this
-- Act; its effect on a claimant is the fact "section 115 excludes me", which is
-- asked as a fact (section 115 is not among the inputs).
-- src:78 | (2) In section 115(1) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (c. 33) (exclusion of certain persons from benefits) in the words preceding paragraph (a), after “Jobseekers Act 1995” insert “ or to state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002 ”.
@ref s 4(2) (src:78)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) -- excluded under section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999` case MEANS
    case's `excluded by section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 as amended by section 4(2)`

-- Section 4(3): where the amount payable by way of state pension credit would
-- (apart from this subsection) be less than a prescribed amount, it shall not be
-- payable except in prescribed circumstances. The amount payable is taken to be the
-- two credits together (section 1(3), last words: "or to both"), the guarantee credit
-- and the savings credit (fork F-08, NOTES.md).
-- src:79 | (3) Where the amount payable by way of state pension credit would (apart from this subsection) be less than a prescribed amount, it shall not be payable except in prescribed circumstances.
@ref s 4(3) (src:79)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed MEANS
        `s 2(2) -- the guarantee credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed
    PLUS `s 3(3) -- the savings credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed

@ref s 4(3) (src:79)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) -- state pension credit is payable` case prescribed MEANS
        `s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed
    AND (   NOT (`s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed LESS THAN prescribed's `prescribed amount below which state pension credit is not payable`)
         OR case's `prescribed circumstances in which an amount below the prescribed amount is payable` )

§§ `5 Income and capital of claimant, spouse etc`

-- Section 5: where the claimant is a member of a couple, the income and capital
-- of the other member shall, except in prescribed circumstances, be treated as the
-- income and capital of the claimant. The exception is an input.
-- src:82 | Where the claimant is a member of a couple , the income and capital of the other member of the couple shall, except in prescribed circumstances, be treated for the purposes of this Act as income and capital of the claimant.
@ref s 5 (src:82)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5 -- the income treated as the claimant's` case MEANS
        `s 15(1) -- income` (case's `income of the claimant`)
    PLUS IF       `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
              AND NOT (case's `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated`)
         THEN `s 15(1) -- income` (case's `income of the other member`)
         ELSE 0

@ref s 5 (src:82)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5 -- the qualifying income treated as the claimant's` case MEANS
        case's `qualifying income of the claimant`
    PLUS IF       `s 17(1) -- couple` (case's household)
              AND NOT (case's `prescribed circumstances in which the income of the other member is not aggregated`)
         THEN case's `qualifying income of the other member`
         ELSE 0

-- Capital: no rule of this Act compares capital with a figure. It matters only
-- through the income it yields (section 15(1)(i), (2)), which the Income record
-- carries already. The aggregation of capital is encoded for completeness.
@ref s 5 (src:82)
GIVEN household IS A Household
      `capital of the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `capital of the other member` IS A NUMBER
      `prescribed circumstances in which the other member's capital is not aggregated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5 -- the capital treated as the claimant's` household `capital of the claimant` `capital of the other member` `prescribed circumstances in which the other member's capital is not aggregated` MEANS
        `capital of the claimant`
    PLUS IF       `s 17(1) -- couple` household
              AND NOT `prescribed circumstances in which the other member's capital is not aggregated`
         THEN `capital of the other member`
         ELSE 0

§§ `17 "entitled" (section 17(1))`

-- Section 17(1) "entitled": entitlement to state pension credit is construed in
-- accordance with (a) this Act, (b) section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement
-- dependent on the making of a claim etc) and (c) section 27 of the Social Security
-- Act 1998 (restrictions on entitlement in certain cases of error). The Act is
-- sections 1 to 5, applied above. (b) and (c) are not among the inputs, so each is a
-- fact: a claim has been made and the conditions of section 1 are met; and no
-- restriction under section 27 applies.
-- src:266 | “entitled”, in relation to state pension credit, shall be construed in accordance with—
-- src:267 | (a) this Act,
-- src:268 | (b) section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to be dependent on making of claim etc), and
-- src:269 | (c) section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 (c. 14) (restrictions on entitlement to benefit in certain cases of error),
-- src:270 | (and, in relation to any other benefit within the meaning of section 1 of the Administration Act or section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998, in accordance with that section or (as the case may be) both of those sections in addition to any other conditions relating to that benefit);
@ref s 17(1) "entitled" (src:266-270)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit` case prescribed MEANS
        "(a) this Act," ... `s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed
    ... "(b) section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to be dependent on making of claim etc), and" ... case's `a claim has been made and the Administration Act section 1 conditions are met`
    AND "(c) section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 (restrictions on entitlement to benefit in certain cases of error)" ... NOT (case's `entitlement restricted by section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998`)

§§ `The Act's answers`

-- The three answers a claimant is asked for, each with the "not covered" outcome
-- where section 12 or section 18A may displace the Act's rules. These are the
-- rules the seat layer calls.
@ref s 1(4); s 12(1); s 18A(5) (src:18)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH AN Answer
`The Act's answer on whether the conditions for entitlement are met` case prescribed MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` case
        THEN `Not covered by this encoding`
        IF `s 1(4) -- entitled to state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed
        THEN `The Act says yes`
        OTHERWISE `The Act says no`

@ref s 17(1) (src:266-270)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH AN Answer
`The Act's answer on whether the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` case prescribed MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` case
        THEN `Not covered by this encoding`
        IF `s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit` case prescribed
        THEN `The Act says yes`
        OTHERWISE `The Act says no`

@ref s 4(3) (src:79)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit under sections 1 to 5` case prescribed MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` case
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `s 4(3) -- state pension credit is payable` case prescribed
        THEN JUST (`s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0

-- The same amount, but only for a claimant who is "entitled" in the sense of section
-- 17(1): the Act's conditions are met AND a claim has been made AND no restriction
-- under section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 applies. The claim and the section 27
-- restriction are applied here, at the top, and not inside sections 2 and 3, where
-- "entitled" is read as the Act's own conditions (fork F-22, NOTES.md). A claimant
-- who has not yet claimed gets the amount above if asked "what would I be entitled
-- to if I claimed?", and nil from this one.
@ref s 17(1) "entitled"; s 4(3) (src:266-270; src:79)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      prescribed IS A Prescribed
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The Act's answer on the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace the Act's rules for the case` case
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`s 17(1) -- entitled to state pension credit` case prescribed)
        THEN JUST 0
        IF `s 4(3) -- state pension credit is payable` case prescribed
        THEN JUST (`s 4(3) -- the amount of state pension credit to which the claimant is entitled` case prescribed)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0
